## Control {{controlId}}: Control Access to Media Containing CUI and Maintain Accountability During Transport

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization controls access to CUI media during transport within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through encryption, chain-of-custody procedures, and transport tracking documented in "Media Transport Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**Digital Media Transport:**
- CUI transmitted electronically uses TLS 1.2+ encryption for all M365 GCC High communications
- Email attachments containing CUI are protected by sensitivity label encryption during transit
- File transfers to external parties require approved secure channels (encrypted email, approved file sharing)

**Physical Media Transport:**
- Physical media (USB drives, hard drives, paper) containing CUI transported using tamper-evident containers
- Chain-of-custody forms document media handler, origin, destination, date/time, and contents description
- Authorized courier services or hand-delivery by cleared personnel required for media transport
- Receipt confirmation required from receiving party within 24 hours

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Maintain media transport log documenting all CUI media movements; quarterly review of transport records
- **Frequency:** Per transport event, quarterly audit
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Media Transport Policy v1.0, Chain of Custody Form MP-005

**Review Frequency:** Quarterly by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine chain-of-custody records, media transport logs, encryption configuration for digital transport, and receipt confirmations.

